; The ONE variable: HORIZONTAL_ALIGNMENT_FILL on an RTL Label. FILL's own RTL
; arm (label.cpp:472-478) reads the shaped PARAGRAPH direction (:470), not
; `rtl_layout` (:471), and `text_direction` decides that. Its default is
; TEXT_DIRECTION_AUTO (label.h:70), NOT inherited, so a Latin paragraph infers
; LTR and the arm never fires: the wrapped Label's LAST line — the one the
; jst_flags skip, so the one that keeps its natural width — must still start at
; x 0. unit-label-rtl-alignment.tscn moves the alignment through the arms that
; DO read the layout direction, so it cannot catch a FILL arm wired to the
; wrong one. Both Labels are 500 wide and centred, so each one's OWN rect
; mirror (control.cpp:1785) is the identity.

